---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REPO } from "../../i18n/ui";
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  page="status"
  eyebrow="Local code and dated trials"
  title="Current implementation"
  description="What runs in the house and in Azure, what the tests enforce, and which implementation gaps remain open."
>
  <p class="lede">
    On 24 August 2026, one activity ran end to end on the deployed system. A parent approved it in
    the browser; the house printed and scanned it, continued from the returned page, and closed it
    at the configured hour. The run exposed four defects while a person observed the printer.
  </p>

  <p>
    On 7 September 2026 the local notebook completed a synthetic activity with two pages, handwriting, reading and continuation in 345.4 measured seconds. The untouched-page control returned blank. Hardware and the deployed revision were not checked, and no deployment was performed.
  </p>

  <h2>Implemented in code</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      The cloud tier, the parent panel and its API, the model router with real credentials, and the
      content-safety gate.
    </li>
    <li>
      The hub services that serve the displays, pull an hourly picture, print, scan and answer a
      button press inside the same HTTP response.
    </li>
    <li>
      The activity format and its structural checks, a second model that rereads activities when the call succeeds and usage limits permit,
      parent approval, whole-page generation, comparison against the blank, and deadline control.
    </li>
    <li>The picture archive, and usage accounting with a per-household cap.</li>
    <li>
      Identity: Entra External ID for parents, a separate workforce app registration with an app
      role for administrators, per-household device keys for the house.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Enforced by tests</h2>

  <p>
    Each boundary below has an automated test. Each test was also mutation-checked by injecting the
    violation and observing the failure.
  </p>

  <table class="numbers descriptions">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Parent approval is separate from generation</th>
        <td>the panel stores decisions on <code>OfferedExperience</code>; the hub retrieves approved records</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Generated output passes through Content Safety</th>
        <td>generation and continuation functions call the gate before returning documents</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">The older Proposal path verifies two seals</th>
        <td>this property does not extend to the current activity and continuation path</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Only one component talks to a model</th>
        <td>import-level check across every package</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Model runtimes stay in the cloud path</th>
        <td>import-level check across device packages and router boundaries</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Readings block implicit copying and pickling</th>
        <td>the HTTP dictionary remains serializable; derived observations and development exceptions are retained</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Interaction excludes engagement mechanics</th>
        <td>a vocabulary check across storage, panel, browser and prompts</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Every push to <code>main</code> runs <code>ruff</code> and the test suite on a clean checkout. The
    workflow records the current test count, failures and elapsed time. It reports independently of
    deployment rather than acting as its release gate.
  </p>

  <h2>Open implementation gaps</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <b>The handheld camera.</b> The physical object is still being assembled and
      <code>vision/</code> is an empty Python package. Camera behavior currently exists as design
      decisions without an implementation or enforcing tests.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>The button panel.</b> The current hardware has one button per display. It closes the paper
      loop but cannot yet capture an answer with several choices.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Memory visibility.</b> A complete view is missing. The system stores profile observations and activity summaries. Administrator development permission lasts 14 days; each permitted reading expires 14 days after its own write.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Activity quality.</b> Building, drawing and investigating can have open outcomes. Checks do not establish comprehension or interest; automatic judges retain false positives. A trial with a person is still needed.
    </li>
    <li><b>Print failure and moment timing.</b> The hub shows <code>instead</code>, but the runner does not execute <code>if_no_page</code>. Consecutive non-collection moments advance without waiting their declared duration.</li>
    <li>
      <b>A second house.</b> Provisioning has been exercised with one household. The installer's
      <code>--install</code> path has not yet been run for another one.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/ILLUSTRATED.md`}>The system in photographs, page by page</a> ·
    <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/ideas`}>what is not built, ranked, each with a cost</a> ·
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/NON-GOALS.md`}>the lines this project will not cross</a>
  </p>
</Base>
